# Exp. 1 (b) b_twoplume3d -- case ${case}  (identical to (a))
# (b): R_icefront/icefrontlength are also non-zero in the two land rows of
# the front column; harmless, the fluxes are multiplied by maskC
# (icefront_thermodynamics.F:143-148), so no melt is computed on land.
# Ice-face fields from gendata (grids.icefront_fields): R_icefront = H in
# the front column, icefrontlength = 1/dx there (icefront_description.tex:12-16).
# Transfer law: pkg/icefront default (icefront_thermodynamics.F:89-97,
# gammaT = max(1e-2 sqrt(1.5e-3) |wVEL|, 1e-4) m/s, gammaS = 5.05e-3 gammaT).
# Ice temperature: linear from ICEFRONTthetaSurface at the surface to 0 degC
# at the front base (icefront_thermodynamics.F:116-123).
# The constants below are the pkg defaults without shelfice
# (icefront_readparms.F:84-88), written out so they are on record.
 &ICEFRONT_PARM01
 ICEFRONTdepthFile='R_icefront.bin',
 ICEFRONTlengthFile='icefrontlength.bin',
 applyIcefrontTendT=.TRUE.,
 applyIcefrontTendS=.TRUE.,
 rhoIcefront=917.,
 ICEFRONTlatentHeat=334.E3,
 ICEFRONTHeatCapacity_Cp=2000.,
 ICEFRONTthetaSurface=-20.,
 ICEFRONTkappa=1.54E-6,
 &
